{"availability":"available","full":"UrbsLab/STREAMLINE","name":"STREAMLINE","description":"Simple Transparent End-To-End Automated Machine Learning Pipeline for Supervised Learning in Tabular Binary Classification Data","category":"Education","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":82,"forks":12,"created":"2022-05-07T01:22:20Z","updated":"2026-09-22T20:29:45Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://urbslab.github.io/STREAMLINE/","topics":["automl-pipeline","binary-classification","data-science","data-visualization","feature-selection","imputation","machine-learning","model-application","statistical-analysis","supervised-learning"],"demo":"https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1ByQuU805GzDGAAGzbUYz8wahnOTUuzvg?usp=sharing","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:06:21.023Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:06:21.023Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:06:21.023Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:06:21.023Z","stars":82,"forks":12}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["STREAMLINE is a parallelizable, customizable, end-to-end automated machine learning pipeline for supervised learning in structured, tabular data. It supports binary classification, multiclass classification, and regression outcomes. It includes exploratory analysis, data processing, imputation, scaling, feature learning, feature importance estimation, feature selection, multiple algorithm model training with hyperparameter optimization, ensemble modeling, comprehensive model evaluation with statistical comparisons, dataset comparison, easy replication, and PDF summary reporting.","STREAMLINE is designed to make rigorous machine learning workflows easier to run, compare, reproduce, and extend. It can be run through Google Colab, a local Jupyter notebook, command-line phase runners, or configuration files that execute the full pipeline."],"features":["Phase 1 exposes --onehotencoding. The default keeps historical behavior and expands non-binary categorical features during data processing. Set --onehotencoding 0 when you want Phase 6 to handle raw categorical columns…","Phase 6 then uses --bypassonehotfornativemodels and --nativecategoricalmodels to decide how raw categoricals are prepared. If Phase 1 metadata shows onehotencoding=False, Phase 6 only runs models listed in…","Phase 6 also writes Optuna trial accounting to /models/optunatrials/optunatrials.csv and includes the same trial summary in each per-CV metrics JSON. This records how many trials actually ran and completed within the…","By default, Phase 6 reruns requested model/CV jobs and overwrites existing model artifacts. Use --skipcompletedmodels 1 on the P6 CLI, or skipcompletedmodels = True in [p6] config settings, for recovery runs that skip…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/UrbsLab/STREAMLINE/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4a33d646f5fd666fb6b198acccf4e9c030154c0b2b227bae65bc4f5e8d010803","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:06:21.369Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:06:21.369Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"STREAMLINE is a parallelizable, customizable, end-to-end automated machine learning pipeline for supervised learning in structured, tabular data. It supports binary classification, multiclass classification, and regression outcomes. It includes exploratory analysis, data processing, imputation, scaling, feature learning, feature importance estimation, feature selection, multiple algorithm model training with hyperparameter optimization, ensemble modeling, comprehensive model evaluation with statistical comparisons, dataset comparison, easy replication, and PDF summary reporting.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/UrbsLab/STREAMLINE/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"4a33d646f5fd666fb6b198acccf4e9c030154c0b2b227bae65bc4f5e8d010803","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/UrbsLab/STREAMLINE/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:06:21.369Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-